## The Business Plan

Revival Creek Homesteader is being designed as a TOS Creations original game with a player-friendly purchasing model.

Our current proposed approach is:

**14 days free to experience the game, followed by a one-time $9.99 permanent unlock.**

There would be no required annual subscription and no automatic charge when the trial expires.

Players who choose to purchase would retain their existing world and progress.

Optional expansion bundles are also planned for home customization, farming equipment, business improvements, vehicles and additional lifestyle experiences.

The goal is to make players want more because they enjoy what the game offers—not because the basic experience is intentionally frustrating or incomplete.

These commercial features remain in the planning stage and may be refined before release.

---

## What Comes Next?

Our next major development objective is to begin turning the existing farmhouse into a usable home.

That means moving from an exterior building to a structure Pete can actually enter, explore, repair and customize.

Future construction will build on the property ownership, purchasing and object-placement systems developed during these first two weeks.

From there, we can begin introducing more meaningful farming activities, equipment, livestock, businesses and community development.

Revival Creek Homesteader is still early in development. Much of the larger gameplay vision remains ahead of us.

But in the first nine days of hands-on Unity work, the project has progressed from an empty landscape into a playable rural environment with driving, interactive buildings, purchasing, construction, property ownership and persistent player progress.

### The TOS Creations Philosophy

**Simple to control. Challenging to build. Rewarding to master.**

Revival Creek is about freedom, creativity, hard work and opportunity.

The challenge should come from developing a homestead, running a business, managing a farm, earning a living and helping a forgotten town grow.

It should never come from struggling to move a simple fence panel.

**The goal isn't simply to rebuild a town. It's to give players the freedom to build a life.**

