# Revival Creek Homesteader
## Development Journey — The Town Comes to Life

**November 10–15, 2026 | TOS Creations**

### Week 2 Continued — November 10–14
#### Turning a Homestead into a Home

During the second week of hands-on development, Revival Creek Homesteader began evolving from an explorable countryside into an increasingly interactive world.

Our focus expanded beyond fences, gates, hardware supplies and property boundaries.

We wanted buildings that players could actually enter, explore, improve and eventually make their own.

**A Functional Farmhouse**

One of our biggest milestones was converting the original farmhouse from a solid exterior structure into a usable home.

The farmhouse received a working front door, walkable ground-floor rooms, interior walls, flooring and lighting.

The layout includes a living room, kitchen/dining area, bedroom or workroom, utility/bathroom area and reserved space for future stairs.

The original exterior appearance was preserved, including its weathered siding, windows, roof and porch.

For the first time, Pete could walk through his front door and explore his own home.

**The Beginning of Home Renovation**

Next came our first working renovation tools.

Players could select interior wall and floor surfaces, preview different finishes and see how improvements would look before committing.

Initial choices included muted wall colors and practical flooring materials suited to an older country farmhouse.

Renovation supplies were connected to the existing in-game economy.

Testing revealed that requiring players to travel to Community Hardware for every small purchase interrupted the building experience.

That led to an important improvement: **Buy & Apply and Buy & Build**.

Players can now preview a project, purchase exactly the materials they're missing, confirm the cost and complete the work without leaving the location.

Community Hardware remains available for traditional in-person shopping.

This became an important development principle:

**Make ordinary actions intuitive. Make meaningful accomplishments challenging.**

**Improving Player Controls**

We also refined instructional panels, camera control and menu interactions.

Players can dismiss lessons, collapse status displays, use clickable controls and return to normal exploration without unnecessary interruptions.

These changes are helping establish a consistent interface that can eventually support both computer and mobile gameplay.

---

### Week 3 — November 15, 2026
#### Building a Town with History

With the core construction and renovation systems established, attention shifted toward creating the larger community originally envisioned for Revival Creek.

The goal was no longer simply to add buildings.

It was to make the world resemble a once-thriving rural town with homes, businesses, farms, roads and a history worth discovering.

**The Residential Neighborhood Expands**

Seven new residential exteriors, designated H1 through H7, have been created and visually reviewed.

Each house has its own architectural style and personality:

- **H1 — Timber Cottage:** A modest, traditional weathered home.
- **H2 — Family Bungalow:** A broader single-story residence with a low roof and offset porch.
- **H3 — Two-Story Village Home:** A traditional family house with a pitched roof and deeper garden lot.
- **H4 — Brick Family Home:** A sturdy older residence with aged masonry and faded trim.
- **H5 — Worker's Cottage:** A smaller, more neglected home with faded siding and selective window boarding.
- **H6 — Timber Family Home:** A larger house with an attached side wing and practical garden space.
- **H7 — Country Cottage:** A distinctive home with a generous covered porch and rear utility extension.

Together with Pete's farmhouse and the two original neighborhood homes, Revival Creek now contains **ten residential buildings**.

The new homes have stable property identities, driveway access and reserved garden areas.

Their interiors, ownership opportunities and future resident activities remain in development.

These homes represent the beginning of a much larger residential community—not a limit on how many people Revival Creek may eventually accommodate.

**Making Exploration Easier**

As the town expanded, traveling repeatedly from the farmhouse to the northern neighborhood became inconvenient during testing.

A new starting-location selector was introduced.

Developers can now choose **MY FARM** or **TOWN** when beginning a Unity test session, with Pete and his pickup appearing together at the selected location.

This allows quicker review of new development without changing saved game progress.

---

### A Living World — Real Time, Real Weather

One of Revival Creek's original design requirements has always been that its world should continue existing whether a player is logged in or not.

During this development period, we established the technical foundations for that experience.

**A Real-World Clock**

Revival Creek now has a real-time world clock based on actual calendar dates.

The system measures elapsed time across game sessions and supports future offline progression.

When a player returns after several days, the world will reflect the real date rather than advancing only when someone plays.

The future goal is for crops, lawns, farm activities and community life to respond appropriately to that elapsed time.

**A Home in West Virginia**

We selected a fictional Appalachian valley near Beckley, West Virginia, as Revival Creek's real-world geographic reference.

The town uses Eastern Time and connects to National Weather Service observations and forecasts.

Every player in the shared Revival Creek world is intended to experience the same local time, seasons and weather.

**Weather Comes to Life**

Our first environmental milestones introduced:

- Real-time sunlight and daylight transitions
- Sunrise, sunset and nighttime appearance
- Cloud conditions informed by actual observations
- Visible rain and snowfall
- Shelter behavior around supported buildings and vehicles
- A clickable Weather Center with current conditions and forecasts
- Development controls for testing weather without changing the real-world clock

During personal review, nighttime snowfall became one of the most satisfying visual improvements.

**Wet Ground and Snow Coverage**

Environmental development continued with realistic ground wetness and initial snow coverage.

A small test area near Pete's farmhouse can now display damp ground, light and heavier snow coverage, and gradual visual melting.

Testing also revealed an interface conflict that prevented snow coverage from appearing. Correcting it allowed snow to become visible on the farmhouse roof and ground.

These systems are currently visual pilots.

Full-town coverage, long-term accumulation, historical weather reconstruction and effects on farming are still planned.

Our long-term goal remains unchanged: weather should leave meaningful evidence in the world, even while players are away.

---

### Main Street Begins to Grow

A thriving town needs more than houses.

Revival Creek already contained Community Hardware, a diner, grocery store, garage and barber shop.

Our commercial expansion began with **Revival Pharmacy**.

**Revival Pharmacy**

The new pharmacy was designed as an aging brick storefront with large display windows, a recessed entrance, faded signage and modest signs of abandonment.

After its exterior was approved, the building received a functional entrance and a basic walkable interior.

Players can now open the door, enter the vacant building, explore and leave.

The pharmacy remains closed as a business, awaiting future restoration and activation.

This marked an important development milestone:

**A building can be abandoned without being inaccessible.**

We intend to expand this approach throughout Revival Creek, allowing players to explore properties and discover their stories while keeping ownership and renovation rights separate.

**Our First Townsperson**

Community Hardware also received its first character: a clerk stationed behind the counter.

Players can approach the clerk, start a conversation and access the existing shopping system.

The clerk currently offers introductory dialogue about Revival Creek and advice for newcomers.

This begins establishing something especially important to the project: a community with people, personalities, memories and stories.

---

### The Story Behind Revival Creek

Development has also expanded into the deeper history of the town.

Our narrative direction centers on a community that once prospered through farming, local businesses, a working mill and the remarkable creek flowing through its valley.

Over time, the town declined, its businesses closed and families moved away.

Years later, a man named Pete saw an opportunity to bring the forgotten community back to life.

The creek will be central to that story.

Its clear water, future irrigation potential and possible water-powered operations connect the town's history to its restoration.

We envision an optional, substantial opening story, followed by discoveries, journal entries and conversations that players can revisit whenever they wish.

Players who enjoy storytelling will be able to explore the town's past.

Those who prefer building, farming and business development will be free to concentrate on those activities.

Both experiences will be part of the same world.

---

### What's Coming Next?

The next development priorities include:

- Additional historic Main Street businesses, beginning with the old village bakery
- More reusable building interiors and accessible entrances
- Expanded neighborhood and agricultural districts
- Town-wide snow and wet-ground coverage
- Persistent weather effects based on recorded conditions
- A more substantial, visually pristine creek supporting future irrigation and water-powered activities
- Farming, crops, livestock and ongoing property maintenance
- Additional residents, conversations and story discoveries
- Shared renovation systems across residential and commercial properties
- A scalable foundation for player accounts and individually owned properties

Our long-term vision is a large, persistent virtual community that continues evolving around the clock.

Players will be able to choose a home, restore property, develop fields, pursue livelihoods and help bring a forgotten town back to life.

### Our Development Philosophy

Revival Creek Homesteader is being created carefully, one tested milestone at a time.

We are not rushing toward release.

Every new system must serve the larger experience: a believable rural world where players have meaningful freedom, where their choices matter and where their accomplishments feel earned.

**Simple to Control. Challenging to Build. Rewarding to Master.**

