# Revival Creek Homesteader
## Development Journey — Weekly Update
**November 15–21, 2026**

### A Town Begins to Come Alive

This week marked one of the most significant transformations yet for *Revival Creek Homesteader*.

Development shifted toward creating a more immersive Appalachian environment and bringing the town's abandoned buildings to life.

What began as a relatively flat landscape with a small creek has evolved into a growing countryside with rolling hills, wooded ridges, flowing water, farmland, and a town filled with traces of its past.

The goal remains the same: create a living community where players can restore homes, reopen businesses, work the land, and help bring a once-thriving Appalachian town back to life.

### A New Landscape for Revival Creek

One of the biggest accomplishments this week was the complete change in direction for the creek and surrounding landscape.

The original small creek was replaced in the developing world with a much more substantial waterway.

The new creek now extends for approximately 850 metres through connected sections of the playable countryside, featuring natural bends, sloping banks, rocks, gravel, and moving blue-green water.

The surrounding landscape also received a major transformation.

Rolling terrain, wooded hillsides, varied grass and soil textures, roadside vegetation, and hundreds of additional trees have given the countryside a more authentic Appalachian appearance.

Revival Creek is beginning to feel like a place that belongs in the hills of West Virginia.

### Farming Takes Root

Agriculture also became a visible part of the world this week.

Three new fields were created in the northern countryside, representing freshly plowed land, planted crops, and early growth.

A corn-growth system now includes five visual stages, from prepared soil to mature plants.

Pete also received his own starter field near the farmhouse, complete with cultivated soil, planting rows, and growing corn.

These are the early foundations for future farming gameplay, where planting, weather, growing seasons, irrigation, and harvesting will become part of everyday life.

### Two New Businesses Join the Town

Revival Creek's commercial district expanded with two additional properties.

**Creek County Farm Equipment** brings a rural sales and service building, tractor and trailer displays, a workshop area, and equipment storage to the outskirts of town.

**Revival Motor Sales** introduces a modest used-car dealership with an office, older vehicle displays, and a gravel sales lot.

Both businesses remain closed, waiting for the possibility of future restoration.

### Community Hardware Gets Stocked

The town's only operating business, Community Hardware, also received a significant interior upgrade.

The store now includes more than 160 physical merchandise displays, featuring tools, fasteners, paint supplies, gardening equipment, animal feed, fencing materials, and other household hardware.

The existing store clerk and purchasing system remain functional.

Community Hardware is becoming an important part of the town's restoration economy—a place where players can obtain the supplies needed to repair and rebuild.

### Discovering the Town's Past

Several previously empty buildings were furnished with aging furniture, abandoned equipment, and remnants of their former occupants.

New interior details were added to:

- The old diner
- The barber shop
- H5 Workers Cottage
- The grocery store
- Revival Pharmacy
- Old Village Bakery
- The historic Five-and-Dime
- Old Town Garage
- H4 Brick Family Home

Each location has its own character, from dusty restaurant booths and vintage barber equipment to old garage tools, household furniture, and forgotten merchandise.

These buildings are not yet restored or reopened.

Instead, they offer a glimpse into the community that existed before its decline.

### Building on a Stronger Foundation

Another important accomplishment has been maintaining these improvements within an increasingly integrated game world.

Pete can continue walking, driving his pickup, exploring buildings, purchasing supplies, and visiting the countryside while new locations are added.

Weather, time, construction, renovation, and other existing systems remain part of the development.

The larger environmental changes have also established a clearer visual direction for the project.

There is still plenty of work ahead, including completing the northern creek, refining vegetation and landscapes, expanding the farming systems, and developing the restoration activities that will eventually allow players to rebuild the community.

But the difference is becoming visible.

### Looking Ahead

Revival Creek Homesteader is still in active development, but the vision is taking shape.

Future work will focus on making the existing environment more interactive, bringing restoration mechanics into furnished buildings, expanding the town, and gradually introducing the people and activities that will make Revival Creek feel alive.

The ultimate goal is not simply to create buildings and scenery.

It is to create a place with history, opportunity, and a future shaped by the players who choose to restore it.

**Revival Creek is beginning to look like the town it was always meant to become.**

*Every home has a history. Every business has a purpose. Every restoration brings Revival Creek one step closer to life.*

— **TOS Creations**

